                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "413a5808-be36-3f3c-b421-af0bc03a2d51",
                        "entry_id": "3f47f211-d1e4-30db-b804-c15b5c40c028",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A condition marked by the accumulation of adipose (fatty) tissue."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7078f25-e48d-4702-a1bd-bf98fb7ca6f0",
                                "sense_id": "413a5808-be36-3f3c-b421-af0bc03a2d51",
                                "text": "These adiposes are etiologically divisible into two types; those, on the one hand, which constitute a phenomenon of hypo- or athyroidea; and, those, on the other hand, which are sequela to hypoplasias and to functional errors in the germinal organs (castration, genital infantilism, etc)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6478b2a3-a8d5-45a2-bfc6-c076a8484fac",
                                "sense_id": "413a5808-be36-3f3c-b421-af0bc03a2d51",
                                "text": "2004, Günther Wittlinger, Hildegard Wittlinger, Textbook of Dr. Vodders: Manual Lymph Drainage, Volume 1: Basic Course, 7th Edition, Complementary Medicine Series, page 92,\nOne should always differentiate between adiposis and panniculopathia-oedemato-fibrosclerotica (the so-called cellulite)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c42dd7ff-0e97-4f33-b44d-1a2975a2a426",
                                "sense_id": "413a5808-be36-3f3c-b421-af0bc03a2d51",
                                "text": "The site of the presystolic activation and delayed conduction along the reentrant circuit have been shown to have significant abnormalities such as fibrosis, adiposis, and degeneration of the myocardium. The scattered myocyte islets in the extensive adiposis and/or fibrosis can form an electrical maze around the surgical suture area."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d11ba71-0653-4cc8-8147-dbd527750649",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f47f211-d1e4-30db-b804-c15b5c40c028",
                        "source_sense_id": "413a5808-be36-3f3c-b421-af0bc03a2d51",
                        "source_sense_description": "accumulation of adipose tissue",
                        "target_lang_word": "adipose",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "adipose",
